Everyone settle.

430
00:42:22.250 --> 00:42:25.210
I have a proposal for the assembly.

431
00:42:30.330 --> 00:42:33.040
We send a search party
to the surface to find my dad.

432
00:42:33.130 --> 00:42:34.290
To the surface?

433
00:42:34.380 --> 00:42:35.850
We can spare
four people from farm duty

434
00:42:35.880 --> 00:42:37.290
for up to two weeks.

435
00:42:37.380 --> 00:42:38.620
even with our dwindled numbers.

436
00:42:38.670 --> 00:42:41.000
Sorry. Lucy. but you're talking about

437
00:42:41.080 --> 00:42:43.170
opening the outer vault door?

438
00:42:43.250 --> 00:42:44.920
Just for under a minute.

439
00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:46.790
Okay? It's just enough time to--

440
00:42:46.880 --> 00:42:49.250
Okay. I-I know we're just...
we're brainstorming here.

441
00:42:49.330 --> 00:42:51.210
and there's no bad ideas
in a brainstorm...

442
00:42:51.290 --> 00:42:52.810
- Maybe for you.
- ...but that's not something

443
00:42:52.830 --> 00:42:53.920
that we ever do

444
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:55.880
or have ever done. never. ever. ever.

445
00:42:55.960 --> 00:42:57.040
I-I know. I know that.

446
00:42:57.130 --> 00:43:00.540
I know we're all hurting right now.

447
00:43:00.630 --> 00:43:02.170
but our first priority

448
00:43:02.250 --> 00:43:05.920
has to be to maintain
the security of this vault.

449
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.790
That means not opening any of our doors.

450
00:43:08.880 --> 00:43:09.960
Well said. Betty.

451
00:43:10.040 --> 00:43:11.790
Yes. thank you. Betty.

452
00:43:11.880 --> 00:43:13.080
Okay. let's move on.

453
00:43:13.170 --> 00:43:15.170
They don't want to find Dad.

454
00:43:16.920 --> 00:43:19.380
If they did. they wouldn't
get to be in charge.

455
00:44:16.880 --> 00:44:18.210
Hey. Davey.

456
00:44:18.290 --> 00:44:19.500
- Hey.
- How's your day going?

457
00:44:20.500 --> 00:44:22.460
Bad as everyone else's.

458
00:45:12.750 --> 00:45:13.920
Hold the elevator.

459
00:45:28.290 --> 00:45:29.290
Take care of Norm

460
00:45:29.380 --> 00:45:31.170
till I'm back. okay?

461
00:45:32.710 --> 00:45:34.630
I can't.

462
00:45:34.710 --> 00:45:36.880
I'm going with you.

463
00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:39.040
- Chet--
- What you're doing is insane.

464
00:45:39.130 --> 00:45:40.790
You don't even know which way to go.

465
00:45:40.880 --> 00:45:42.750
It isn't like the vault out there.

466
00:45:42.830 --> 00:45:43.830
It's big.

467
00:45:49.420 --> 00:45:50.830
Chet...

468
00:45:50.920 --> 00:45:52.750
I'm not letting anyone else

469
00:45:52.830 --> 00:45:54.290
get hurt on my behalf.

470
00:45:54.380 --> 00:45:55.920
Okay?

471
00:46:01.290 --> 00:46:02.880
Lucy.

472
00:46:04.830 --> 00:46:06.960
Okay. There we go.

473
00:46:16.330 --> 00:46:18.880
I just tranq'd him.

474
00:46:18.960 --> 00:46:21.000
And I'll do the same to you
if you try to follow me.

475
00:46:22.290 --> 00:46:23.500
I'm too chicken.

476
00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:24.880
Thanks.

477
00:46:56.170 --> 00:46:57.920
I'm bringing him home.

478
00:47:33.880 --> 00:47:35.080
Stop!

479
00:47:35.170 --> 00:47:36.500
Lucy!

480
00:47:36.580 --> 00:47:38.880
Are you mad?

481
00:47:38.960 --> 00:47:41.670
Young lady. come back here right away!

482
00:47:43.290 --> 00:47:44.790
Lucy!

483
00:47:46.920 --> 00:47:48.750
Lucy. no!

484
00:47:55.540 --> 00:47:57.380
That didn't work.

485
00:49:46.580 --> 00:49:48.830
Okey do key.

486
00:50:19.130 --> 00:50:22.130
We have given you a name.

487
00:50:25.040 --> 00:50:26.330
Food.

488
00:50:26.420 --> 00:50:28.460
Education.

489
00:50:28.540 --> 00:50:30.500
A place in the world.

490
00:50:30.580 --> 00:50:32.500
So...

491
00:50:33.630 --> 00:50:35.960
…we expect you to give us

492
00:50:36.040 --> 00:50:38.540
the truth.

493
00:50:38.630 --> 00:50:40.710
Why did you join the Brotherhood?

494
00:50:41.920 --> 00:50:44.380
To hurt the people who hurt me.

495
00:50:54.040 --> 00:50:57.290
I understand you're
a friend of Aspirant Dane.

496
00:50:57.380 --> 00:50:59.380
Yes.

497
00:50:59.460 --> 00:51:01.330
You're aware of their injury?

498
00:51:01.420 --> 00:51:02.580
Yes.

499
00:51:02.670 --> 00:51:05.080
Do you know who did it?

500
00:51:07.710 --> 00:51:09.710
No.

501
00:51:13.790 --> 00:51:16.460
Your fellow aspirants say it was you.

502
00:51:19.960 --> 00:51:22.460
No. I…

503
00:51:22.540 --> 00:51:24.290
I-I wouldn't...

504
00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:26.080
Why not?

505
00:51:26.170 --> 00:51:28.170
Your friend was promoted. you were not.

506
00:51:28.250 --> 00:51:30.540
You have ambitions. don't you?

507
00:51:44.630 --> 00:51:45.750
Speak.

508
00:51:45.830 --> 00:51:47.750
I didn't.

509
00:51:47.830 --> 00:51:50.080
I didn't do it. I did not. I...

510
00:51:58.830 --> 00:52:01.880
I wanted it to happen.
Is that wrong?

511
00:52:07.080 --> 00:52:09.250
Yes.

512
00:52:11.040 --> 00:52:13.040
Yes.

513
00:52:13.130 --> 00:52:14.880
Violence...

514
00:52:14.960 --> 00:52:16.710
is merely a tool.

515
00:52:16.790 --> 00:52:20.670
We use it to bring order
to the Wasteland. but

516
00:52:20.750 --> 00:52:25.420
violence against a Brother of Steel

517
00:52:25.500 --> 00:52:27.790
is a sign of weakness.

518
00:52:31.250 --> 00:52:33.290
But are you?

519
00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:37.880
Weak?

520
00:52:41.380 --> 00:52:44.750
I don't want to be. I...

521
00:53:02.920 --> 00:53:04.750
You have anything else to say

522
00:53:04.830 --> 00:53:07.210
in your defense?

523
00:53:19.040 --> 00:53:21.380
I just...

524
00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:25.170
I just...

525
00:53:25.250 --> 00:53:27.630
I-I want to thank you.

526
00:53:35.080 --> 00:53:37.500
For your guidance and...

527
00:53:37.580 --> 00:53:39.420
for giving me a home.

528
00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:42.170
I-I had no place in the world.

529
00:53:42.250 --> 00:53:44.250
So...

530
00:53:47.670 --> 00:53:50.960
…if I can help
the Brotherhood make it better...

531
00:53:53.420 --> 00:53:56.130
...Eden or whatever...

532
00:53:58.540 --> 00:54:01.080
...even if it means giving my own life...

533
00:54:02.420 --> 00:54:04.420
...I'll do it.

534
00:54:12.540 --> 00:54:16.420
And I'd be grateful to the Brotherhood
for giving my life meaning.

535
00:54:20.170 --> 00:54:22.420
Good boy.

536
00:54:25.790 --> 00:54:28.670
Then you will be Knight Titus'

537
00:54:28.750 --> 00:54:30.670
new squire.

538
00:55:01.170 --> 00:55:03.290
It's not so bad.

539
00:55:03.380 --> 00:55:06.420
At least here no one steals your rations.

540
00:55:07.630 --> 00:55:09.710
They said I'll still have
a place at the Brotherhood.

541
00:55:11.170 --> 00:55:13.170
But I heard you got my spot.

542
00:55:19.080 --> 00:55:21.170
You know who did it?

543
00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:25.040
I've narrowed it down
to any one of those assholes.

544
00:55:26.040 --> 00:55:27.380
- Yeah.
- You like that?

545
00:55:27.460 --> 00:55:28.580
- No!
- There you are.

546
00:55:28.670 --> 00:55:30.960
- Yeah!
- Stop it!

547
00:55:31.040 --> 00:55:32.380
He likes it.

548
00:55:32.460 --> 00:55:34.500
They asked if it was you.

549
00:55:41.580 --> 00:55:43.630
Yeah. they asked me the same thing.

550
00:55:46.380 --> 00:55:48.750
I told 'em you wouldn't hurt a fly.

551
00:56:02.500 --> 00:56:04.750
Aspirant Maximus.

552
00:56:04.830 --> 00:56:08.630
It is your most sacred duty
to protect the Brotherhood.

553
00:56:09.670 --> 00:56:14.080
After which. it is your most sacred duty
to protect the mission.

554
00:56:14.170 --> 00:56:18.290
After which. it is your most sacred duty

555
00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:21.880
to protect your lord Knight Titus.

556
00:56:25.040 --> 00:56:27.960
Do you accept?

557
00:56:51.170 --> 00:56:55.830
Our mission comes from the highest clerics

558
00:56:55.920 --> 00:56:59.170
in the Commonwealth.

559
00:56:59.250 --> 00:57:01.380
It is believed

560
00:57:01.460 --> 00:57:03.130
that a denizen

561
00:57:03.210 --> 00:57:05.040
of the Enclave

562
00:57:05.130 --> 00:57:06.670
has escaped.

563
00:57:06.750 --> 00:57:08.830
The Enclave's real?

564
00:57:08.920 --> 00:57:11.500
And that he has with him an object...

565
00:57:12.540 --> 00:57:15.580
...of profound potential...

566
00:57:16.920 --> 00:57:19.750
...to harm our nation

567
00:57:19.830 --> 00:57:21.580
or to save it.

568
00:57:22.580 --> 00:57:26.670
Each knight in this legion

569
00:57:26.750 --> 00:57:31.500
will search a section of the Wilds
for this target.

570
00:57:31.580 --> 00:57:33.250
Brothers...

571
00:57:33.330 --> 00:57:35.750
...we exist

572
00:57:35.830 --> 00:57:38.170
for moments such as these.

573
00:57:38.250 --> 00:57:41.210
Go forth

574
00:57:41.290 --> 00:57:43.330
with honor!

575
00:57:44.580 --> 00:57:46.880
And may the shape of the future

576
00:57:46.960 --> 00:57:49.250
be cut by your sword!

577
00:57:51.040 --> 00:57:53.790
Approximation of the target for your lord.

578
00:58:02.540 --> 00:58:05.380
You're dismissed. Aspirant.

579
00:59:46.670 --> 00:59:48.580
How do we know which grave?

580
00:59:48.670 --> 00:59:50.920
Well. Slim.
we look for the fresh one.

581
00:59:55.790 --> 00:59:58.630
Dom Pedro has our friend
dug up once a year.

582
00:59:58.710 --> 01:00:03.080
Cuts some pieces off
and puts him right back in the ground.

583
01:00:10.630 --> 01:00:12.880
Bingo.

584
01:00:12.960 --> 01:00:14.040
Shit.

585
01:00:14.130 --> 01:00:17.420
You're telling me
this supreme badass we're looking for

586
01:00:17.500 --> 01:00:18.960
is a godforsaken mutant?

587
01:00:19.040 --> 01:00:21.630
Have some respec'.

588
01:00:21.710 --> 01:00:24.790
That's your prospective coworker
you's talking about

589
01:00:24.880 --> 01:00:27.250
and our ticket to a big payoff.

590
01:00:27.330 --> 01:00:28.750
Thought you said you knew this guy.

591
01:00:28.830 --> 01:00:30.710
I said I knew of him.

592
01:00:31.710 --> 01:00:33.580
My pop worked with him once.

593
01:00:33.670 --> 01:00:35.080
Your pop?

594
01:00:35.170 --> 01:00:37.140
How long's this asshole
been moldering in the ground?

595
01:00:37.170 --> 01:00:38.460
How do we know he's not feral?

596
01:00:38.540 --> 01:00:40.420
That is why

597
01:00:40.500 --> 01:00:42.080
we brought...

598
01:00:42.170 --> 01:00:43.790
...our little friend.

599
01:00:43.880 --> 01:00:47.170
A feral ghoul can't abide a chicken.

600
01:00:48.330 --> 01:00:51.170
If he goes for her. we kill him.

601
01:01:04.130 --> 01:01:06.000
Whoa. whoa.

602
01:02:33.500 --> 01:02:36.040
Well. well. well.

603
01:02:36.130 --> 01:02:39.580
Why. is this an Amish production
of The Count of Monte Cristo or...

604
01:02:39.670 --> 01:02:43.830
just the weirdest circle jerk
I've ever been invited to?

605
01:02:52.580 --> 01:02:54.420
Welcome back.

606
01:02:54.500 --> 01:02:55.540
I'm Honcho.

607
01:02:55.630 --> 01:02:56.880
Now. you don't even know us--

608
01:02:56.960 --> 01:02:58.380
No.

609
01:02:58.460 --> 01:03:00.130
I do not.

610
01:03:13.040 --> 01:03:14.920
Does that count?

611
01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:17.290
Sh-Should I shoot him?

612
01:03:17.380 --> 01:03:19.830
Would you shut the fuck up?

613
01:03:19.920 --> 01:03:21.170
We...

614
01:03:21.250 --> 01:03:23.460
we got a proposition for you.

615
01:03:23.540 --> 01:03:25.290
A bounty came down.

616
01:03:25.380 --> 01:03:26.960
A huge one.

617
01:03:27.040 --> 01:03:28.540
Enough to be a...

618
01:03:28.630 --> 01:03:31.540
last score for me and whoever's with me.

619
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:36.170
Yeah. Now. somebody made a run...

620
01:03:37.750 --> 01:03:39.290
...from the Enclave.

621
01:03:40.380 --> 01:03:43.210
Well. what makes you think
I'd give a good goddamn about that?

622
01:03:43.290 --> 01:03:47.210
It ain't where they's running from
I figured you'd be interested in.

623
01:03:47.290 --> 01:03:48.670
It's where they's running to.

624
01:03:49.830 --> 01:03:52.670
That witch Moldaver.

625
01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:55.670
In California.

626
01:03:56.920 --> 01:03:58.670
That's where you from. ain't it?

627
01:04:00.080 --> 01:04:01.880
Originally. I mean.

628
01:04:07.540 --> 01:04:10.380
Now. what the fuck would you know
about where I'm from?

629
01:04:13.170 --> 01:04:16.710
Well. that don't sound
like gratitude. do it. boys?

630
01:04:18.080 --> 01:04:20.170
How about we put you
right back in that hole

631
01:04:20.250 --> 01:04:24.170
so Dom Pedro can have his fun with you
for the next 30 years?

632
01:04:33.130 --> 01:04:35.500
Well. I tell you what. boys.

633
01:04:35.580 --> 01:04:37.920
whenever somebody says...

634
01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:42.670
...they're doing one last job. that
usually means their heart's not in it.

635
01:04:42.750 --> 01:04:44.670
Probably never was.

636
01:04:46.920 --> 01:04:48.420
But for me.

637
01:04:48.500 --> 01:04:50.670
well...

638
01:04:50.750 --> 01:04:53.040
I do this shit for the love of the game.

639
01:05:31.460 --> 01:05:33.330
You right. friend.
about one thing.

640
01:05:36.290 --> 01:05:37.830
This right here

641
01:05:37.920 --> 01:05:40.750
was your last job.

642
01:05:40.830 --> 01:05:43.540
My paycheck wasn't quite
what you expected. but...

643
01:05:43.630 --> 01:05:45.920
well. you know what they say.

644
01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:47.920
Us cowpokes...

645
01:05:55.130 --> 01:05:57.710
...we take it as it comes.

646
01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:13.000
Subtitles by ZigMedia
